  "body": "## What changed\n\n`assets/posts/tormach.cps` no longer refuses an A that changes inside an operation on an A-about-X machine. It now posts it as wrapped (simultaneous) A, based on mkinney's four PathPilot Hub readings on #796 (v2.14.4, 770MX SIM, 4th axis on):\n\n- **A is cumulative.** PathPilot treats A as plain degrees with no rollover (A350 -> `G1 A10` turned back 340 deg). Each target is the nearest equivalent of the held angle: 179 -> 181, 359 -> 361, never back through 0. A count past the stated travel is refused by name.\n- **A turning X Y Z feed is G93.** `F = 1 / t`, where t (min) = max((the tip's path relative to the part + one rounding step) / the programmed feed, the posted |dA| / the stated A rate). F is floored to 0.001, so rounding only ever slows a move. Neither the cutting feed nor the A rate is exceeded. The rate comes from `rotaryRate` (#885).\n- **An A-only feed stays G94**, with F in deg/min under the same time law (Hub reading 4). Feeds that don't turn A are unchanged. G94 is restated before any motion that is not a G93 feed and at every section end.\n- **Turning moves are split onto their segment.** The machine moves XYZ in a line while A turns, so the tip relative to the part bows off the stream's segment. Each turning move (rapids too) is split into 2^k pieces until the bow is within 0.005 mm (at most 256 pieces, else refused by name).\n- **A is reset between operations:** as before (#785), each section restates its first A as -180..180 after `G53 G0 Z0`, so a wrap that ended at A300 unwinds at the top of Z.\n- **Refused by name:** a machine file with no A rate (\"states no A feed rate\"), a count past the travel (\"A counts on through 360 (PathPilot does not roll A over)\"), an arc / canned cycle / probe move that would turn A, a turning move from an unknown start, and a move that still bows after 256 splits.\n- `assets/machines/tormach-770mx-microarc4.mch` now states A `max_normal_speed` 360 deg/min. That is the rate the Hub ran as asked. It is conservative: no Tormach rate could be cited with confidence.\n- Docs: the tester-kit README, `first-4axis-part.md` and `continuous-4-axis.md` (with its site test), plus `docs/decisions/796-tormach-wrapped-a.md`. The kit's `.camproj` was re-saved by its own test, so it carries the A rate.\n\nFork branch based on upstream `main` at 4e8616b (not a cut tag), so the #885 rule and the current post are in.\n\n## How tested\n\nNew pins in `crates/app/tests/tormach_wrapped_a.rs` (10 tests):\n- `a_long_xyz_move_takes_its_time_from_the_feed`: `G93 G1 X50 Y0 Z0 A1 F11.999` (50 mm at F600)\n- `a_mostly_rotary_move_takes_its_time_from_the_a_rate`: `G1 X51 Y0 Z0 A91 F4` (90 deg at 360 deg/min)\n- `g94_comes_back_before_an_xyz_only_feed_and_a_turns_in_deg_per_min`\n- `a_counts_on_through_180_and_360_never_back_through_0`\n- `the_next_operation_resets_a_at_the_safe_z`\n- `a_section_that_ends_in_g93_restates_g94_before_m5`\n- `a_turning_move_off_the_axis_is_split_onto_its_chord`: every posted point, turned back into the part, lies on the stream's chord, and each piece is held to both rates\n- `a_count_past_the_travel_is_refused_by_name`, `a_machine_with_no_a_rate_is_refused_by_name`, `the_microarc_states_its_a_rate`\n\nGolden: `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/tormach/wrap_rotary_parallel_microarc4.nc` is the microARC kit's job plus a real Rotary Parallel (1/8\" ball) on the bar. It is pinned by `microarc_test_part::a_wrapped_op_on_the_test_part_posts_wrapped_a`, which replaces `a_wrapped_op_on_the_test_part_is_refused_by_name` and also checks A unwrapping, G93 on every turning XYZ feed, G94 elsewhere, and G94 at the section end.\n\nUpdated: `tormach_fourth_axis::an_a_that_changes_inside_an_operation_posts_wrapped_a` (was `..._is_refused`). In `fourth_axis_pose`, the two fanuc tests on the microARC file now place A with a rapid first, because that file now states an A rate and the #885 rule asks for it. The recorded `rotary.refusal` golden for tormach (tilt-head machine) now names the B tilt refusal instead.\n\nGate (macOS, debug, targeted - `cargo xtask gate quick` plans every app suite because a new golden is shared test input, so the touched suites ran instead): every camcraft-app test binary that names Tormach / the microARC (69 binaries, incl. `tormach_wrapped_a`, `microarc_test_part`, `tormach_fourth_axis`, `fourth_axis_pose`, `first_4axis_part`, `index_swing`, `tormach_post`, `rotary_feed_cap`, `recorded_post_streams`) and every camcraft-post binary that names Tormach or the recorded streams (45 binaries, incl. `script_tormach`, `explain_tormach`, `recorded_streams`): all green. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app` on the four changed test files `-D warnings`: clean. `site/tests/test_first_4axis_part.py`: the updated tests pass; `test_machine_and_post_are_the_shipped_ones` fails the same way on upstream main (machine name not in `posting.rs`), not touched here.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No real cut, and this exact program has not been run in the Hub. The readings cover single test moves only.\n- PathPilot's A soft limits. The file keeps -360..360, and a wrap past it is refused.\n\n## Hub check (before trusting it on the 770MX + microARC 4)\n\nRun slowly (feed override 25-50 %, single block for the first lines), with the tool lifted 1\" above the work offset (air cut):\n1. Post the golden's WRAP op (or `wrap_rotary_parallel_microarc4.nc`) and load it in the Hub 770MX SIM with the 4th axis on. Confirm it loads with no error on `G93` / `G94` lines and no \"F word missing\".\n2. Watch the A DRO on a stretch that passes 180 (e.g. line 1393 of the golden, A180 -> A185.757): A must keep counting up, never swing back through 0.\n3. Time one long G93 line against its F (time = 1/F min). Check one A-only `G1 A.. F360` runs at 6 deg/s.\n4. Confirm the control is back in G94 after the WRAP op (Status tab / the next op's feeds run at their ipm).\n5. Check PathPilot's A soft limits (jog A past +360 / -360 in the SIM) and report them on #796, so the machine file's travel can be stated.\n6. Only then air-cut on the real machine at a low override, the bar in the chuck, a hand on feed hold.\n\nChangelog: Tormach PathPilot post: continuous (wrapped) A on the microARC 4 - A counts on past 360, turning feeds in G93 held to the feed and the stated A rate (360 deg/min); refused by name when the machine states no A rate or the count passes the A travel (#796)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #796\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
